diff --git a/docs/docker-deployment.md b/docs/docker-deployment.md
index f6eca78..df009ae 100644
--- a/docs/docker-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/docker-deployment.md
@@ -92,6 +92,17 @@ Less commonly, you might also need to set some of the following:
 
 You can find out more about all these settings in the [Rails Action Mailer documentation](https://guides.rubyonrails.org/action_mailer_basics.html#action-mailer-configuration).
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Set `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` to your Web Push VAPID key pair on both the app and background-job processes.
+Keep the pair stable across deployments: changing it requires people to subscribe again.
+Only the public key is sent to browsers; keep the private key in your deployment's secrets.
+
+Push notifications require HTTPS (localhost also works for development) and a running background-job worker.
+People opt in from **Notification Settings** on each browser/device they want to receive notifications on.
+On iOS, install Fizzy on the Home Screen first; the settings page includes browser-specific help.
+The push control is hidden when either key is missing.
+
 #### Base URL
 
 Fizzy needs to know the public URL of your instance so it can generate correct links in certain situations (like when sending emails).
